// Typecheck config for test code: the `test/` eval harness and e2e suites, plus
// every colocated `*.test.ts(x)` under `src/`.
//
// The root `tsconfig.json` is `include: ["src/**/*"]`, so until this existed
// NOTHING under `test/` was typechecked by `pnpm typecheck` or by CI. That is the
// entire LongMemEval / recall / extraction / consolidation harness: the code every
// measurement in the memory epics is derived from, with no type gate.
//
// It was not theoretical. Widening the exported union `ConsolidationFallbackReason`
// in #803 left `Record<ConsolidationFallbackReason, number>` in
// `createConsolidationFallbackTracker` missing a key — a compile error that `tsc`
// reported nothing about because the file is under `test/`. Only a review bot
// caught it.
//
// Why a separate config rather than widening the root `include`: the root builds
// to CommonJS (`module: "commonjs"`, emitting `dist/`), and `test/` is ESM — it
// uses `import.meta.url` (see `test/memory/src/vault/embeddingCache.ts`), which TS
// rejects under a CommonJS target. So the two trees genuinely need different
// module settings, and `rootDir: "./src"` on the root config cannot cover `test/`
// either.
//
// `moduleResolution: "bundler"` matches how this code actually runs: vitest
// transforms it with esbuild, which resolves extensionless relative imports. Using
// `nodenext` instead would demand explicit `.js` extensions and fail on files that
// run fine today — checking them under rules they are never executed under would
// report problems that do not exist.
//
// The `src/**/*.test.*` globs are here for the same reason `test/**/*` is, and they
// arrived later because the hole was less obvious: the root config's
// `exclude: ["**/*.test.ts", ...]` silently dropped 168 colocated suites, so a test
// whose fixture had drifted out of shape still ran green and still reported nothing.
// That is worse than an uncompiled harness — a suite that passes `{}` where the
// signature grew three required fields keeps its name and stops testing what the
// name claims.
//
// They belong to THIS config, not a widened root `include`, and the reason is the
// same "never executed under those rules" argument as above, with receipts. The root
// targets `es2020`, so `expect(calls.at(-1))` — a normal idiom in these suites, and
// fine on every Node the tests run on — reports TS2550 "Property 'at' does not
// exist". And `rootDir: "./src"` rejects `src/lib/memory/entitySalience.test.ts`
// outright with TS6059, because it imports the shared topic dataset out of
// `test/memory/`. Checking src tests under the root config invents 5 errors in 4
// files that do not exist under the settings vitest actually uses.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // Check only — `dist/` is built from `src/` by the root config.
    "noEmit": true,
    // Widen from the root's "./src" so test/ is in scope.
    "rootDir": ".",
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "target": "es2022",
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  // Non-test `src/` arrives transitively via the imports and is checked as a side
  // effect, which is intended: a `src` change that breaks a call site should fail
  // here. The `*.spec.*` globs match nothing today but mirror
  // `vitest.config.mts`'s include — vitest would run such a file, so tsc should see
  // it the day someone adds one.
  "include": [
    "test/**/*",
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.tsx",
    "src/**/*.spec.ts",
    "src/**/*.spec.tsx"
  ],
  // The root config excludes `**/*.test.ts`; test files are the point here.
  //
  // The five entries below are the pre-existing errors this config would otherwise
  // start reporting in suites that open PRs are mid-rewrite on. Their fixture rot is
  // the same StoredVaultMemory drift fixed everywhere else, but the fixes land on the
  // exact lines those branches are rewriting (#834 rewrites retain.test.ts around
  // both 107 and 576), so fixing them here buys nothing but conflicts. Delete these
  // five lines and fix the 21 errors once both PRs are in — tracked on #820.
  "exclude": [
    // #832 (query decomposition out of recall)
    "src/lib/memory/recall.test.ts",
    "src/lib/memory/recallTool.test.ts",
    "src/lib/memoryVault/searchTool.test.ts",
    // #834 (tool-save via retain)
    "src/lib/memory/retain.test.ts",
    "src/lib/memoryVault/tool.test.ts"
  ]
}
